          "citation": "240 Ariz. 142, 377 P.3d 339 (App. 2016)",
          "court": "Court of Appeals of Arizona",
          "year": 2016,
          "date_decided": "2016-06-09",
          "holding": "The court of appeals held that the electronic records and data DCS maintains in its CHILDS case-management system are public records subject to Arizona's public records law, affirming in part, reversing in part, and remanding.",
          "relevance": "Opens the state data on safety and permanency outcomes that CFSR monitoring measures.",
          "quote": "Under any of the formulations of a public record discussed above, and based on its content, CHILDS is a public record.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/6604368/american-civil-liberties-union-v-arizona-department-of-child-safety/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 6604368
        },
        {
          "case_name": "Griffis v. Pinal County",
          "citation": "215 Ariz. 1, 156 P.3d 418 (2007)",
          "court": "Arizona Supreme Court",
          "year": 2007,
          "date_decided": "2007-04-25",
          "holding": "The Arizona Supreme Court held that purely personal documents of a public officer are not public records but that the custodian's assertion is not conclusive, reversed the superior court, vacated the court of appeals' opinion, and remanded for in camera inspection.",
          "relevance": "Anchors public access to the performance data underlying federal monitoring.",
          "quote": "Arizona law defines \"public records\" broadly and creates a presumption requiring the disclosure of public documents",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/867384/griffis-v-pinal-county/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 867384
        },
        {
          "case_name": "Momox-Caselis v. Donohue",
          "citation": "987 F.3d 835 (9th Cir. 2021)",
          "court": "United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit",
          "year": 2021,
          "date_decided": "2021-02-03",
          "holding": "The Ninth Circuit affirmed summary judgment for the county and its officials in a suit over a foster child's death, holding the family failed to prove deliberate indifference under the special-relationship exception or to establish a Monell claim given the county's licensing and training policies.",
          "relevance": "Illustrates how agency licensing and training records become the evidentiary core of systemic oversight claims.",
          "quote": "The \"special relationship\" exception applies when there is a custodial relationship between the plaintiff and the State, such that the State assumes some responsibility for the plaintiff's safety and well-being.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/4853292/sergio-momox-caselis-v-tara-donohue/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 4853292
        }
